// LLD deliverable: classes, fields, signatures, relationships
abstract class Vehicle { String plate; abstract SpotSize requiredSize(); }
class Car extends Vehicle { SpotSize requiredSize() { return SpotSize.REGULAR; } }

class ParkingLot {                      // HAS-A floors (composition)
    private List<ParkingFloor> floors;
    Optional<ParkingTicket> park(Vehicle v);   // key behaviour
    BigDecimal unpark(ParkingTicket t);
}
```
*The output is concrete classes and signatures — not boxes-and-arrows infrastructure (that's HLD).*

```java
// A Stack is NOT really an ArrayList -- inheriting exposes wrong methods
class Stack<E> extends ArrayList<E> {   // BAD: now callers can add(index, e) into the middle!
    void push(E e) { add(e); }
    E pop() { return remove(size() - 1); }
}
```

```java
class Stack<E> {
    private final List<E> items = new ArrayList<>();  // HAS-A, hidden
    void push(E e) { items.add(e); }
    E pop() { return items.remove(items.size() - 1); }
    // only stack operations are exposed -- no leaking list methods
}
```
*Composition exposes exactly the intended API; inheritance would leak `ArrayList`'s whole surface.*

